Cell["Table of Evaluated Terms", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.810945131807026*^9, 
  3.810945143613596*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"337c3622-ddfa-4797-bf6e-\
53d36fe678b8"],

Cell["\<\
Annoyingly, this arrangement of the terms isn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t very \
popular. Instead scientists usually write out direct expanded expressions in \
terms of the zero-order states. So we\[CloseCurlyQuote]re gonna tabulate \
first, second, and third order correction expressions to make working with \
existing stuff cleaner. We won\[CloseCurlyQuote]t do full expansions of the \
terms, because that\[CloseCurlyQuote]s a pain in the ass, but we\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll get part of the way there.\
\>", "ExpositoryText",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.810945144835349*^9, 3.810945147349616*^9}, {
  3.810945180972519*^9, 3.810945246018744*^9}, {3.8109452930244427`*^9, 
